                <pb facs="0515" n="476" sameAs="frus:frus1969-76v28/pg476"/>

                <head>189. Note From the White House Staff Secretary (Connor) to President Ford<anchor n="1" xml:id="d189-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1976-05-11">May 11, 1976</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <opener>
                    <salute>Mr President:</salute>
                </opener>
                <p rendition="#center">Application for UN Membership
                    by Angola</p>
                <p>Jack Marsh made the following recommendation on the attached memo from Brent Scowcroft:<anchor n="2" xml:id="d189-f2"/>
                    <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“Veto but subject to approval by withdrawal of Cuban troops when and if
                            withdrawal occurs.”<anchor n="3" xml:id="d189-f3"/>
                        </p>
                    </quote>
                </p>
                <p>We are attempting to obtain a reaction on this subject from Tim Austin but this has not been received at
                    this writing.<anchor n="4" xml:id="d189-f4"/>
                </p>
                <p>We have just been notified by the NSC that
                        UN will begin discussion of this subject at
                    10:30 this morning, therefore, this paper requires immediate action.<anchor
                        n="5" xml:id="d189-f5"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#bold">Jim Connor</hi>
                        <anchor n="6" xml:id="d189-f6"/>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d189-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d189-f1-content">
                <p>Source: Ford Library, Staff Secretary’s
                    Office, Presidential Handwriting File, Box 6, Subject File, Countries, Angola.
                    No classification marking.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d189-f2" n="2" xml:id="d189-f2-content">
                <p>
                    <ref target="#d188">Document 188</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d189-f3" n="3" xml:id="d189-f3-content">
                <p>See <ref target="#d191-f4">footnote 4, Document 191</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d189-f4" n="4" xml:id="d189-f4-content">
                <p>Another note from Connor to Ford, May 11, reads: “Just heard from
                        Tim Austin—the feeling from his area
                    is they concur in the recommendation to abstain.” (Ford Library, Staff Secretary’s Office, Presidential Handwriting
                    File, Box 6, Subject File, Countries, Angola)</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d189-f5" n="5" xml:id="d189-f5-content">
                <p>A note from Connor to Scowcroft, May 11, reads: “We have been
                    informed the President gave Ambassador Scranton verbal orders to veto.” (Ibid.)</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d189-f6" n="6" xml:id="d189-f6-content">
                <p>Printed from a copy that bears this typed signature.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
